      "title": "Sentence 3 — temporary support with a passive relative clause",
      "text": "**Original, E:** “A useful lesson can scaffold a difficult task by supplying temporary support that is gradually withdrawn.”\n\n**Plain-English paraphrase:** A lesson can help a learner through a difficult task, then reduce that help as it becomes less necessary.\n\n**Structure:** Main clause + “by” followed by an -ing clause expressing means; a relative clause modifies “support.”\n\n**Main clause:** “A useful lesson can scaffold a difficult task.”\n\n**Dependent clauses:** “supplying temporary support …” is a non-finite clause after “by.” “That is gradually withdrawn” is a defining passive relative clause describing the support.\n\n**Important grammar:** “By supplying” explains how. “Is withdrawn” focuses on removal of support without naming the person removing it. “Can” presents a possibility, not a universal guarantee.\n\n**Useful vocabulary:** scaffold a task; temporary support; gradually withdraw.\n\n**Why it sounds academic:** It gives both the mechanism and the defining feature of a teaching approach.\n\n**New IELTS-style example:** A training programme can develop independence by providing guidance that is gradually reduced.",
